problem-770-s3.c:54:0:high:Flawfinder scanf: The scanf() family's %s operation, without a limit specification, permits buffer overflows (CWE-120, CWE-20). Specify a limit to %s, or use a different input function. If the scanf format is influenceable by an attacker, it's exploitable. (risk 4, buffer)
